# Netlify redirects. One rule per line: from  to  status
# https://docs.netlify.com/manage/routing/redirects/redirect-options/

# g6.html -> whitespace-as-ui-component (slug renamed for SEO)
/guide/g6.html   /guide/whitespace-as-ui-component   301

# NOTE on hiding .html: the reliable way to do this on Netlify is the
# built-in "Pretty URLs" toggle (Site settings > Build & deploy >
# Post processing > Asset optimization), not a custom rule here.
# Netlify's own placeholder syntax doesn't cleanly support a rule like
# "/guide/:slug.html -> /guide/:slug" (a placeholder glued to a literal
# suffix in the same segment isn't part of its documented pattern
# matching), and by default Netlify won't run a rule against a URL that
# already matches a real file on disk (the .html files) unless the rule
# is force-flagged -- so a hand-rolled version of this is easy to get
# subtly wrong. Pretty URLs is Netlify's own tested implementation of
# exactly this behavior, so it doesn't have that risk.
